Parts of futon's engine are adapted from, or follow measurements published
by, aikit (https://github.com/townsendmerino/aikit), used under the MIT
License:

  - native/mathf32.go: the float32 exp kernel (Cephes minimax with
    magic-number range reduction), from aikit linalg/exp.go.
  - native/kernel.go parallelTiles: splitting GEMM work by output column so
    each worker streams only its slice of the weights, after aikit
    encoder/parallel.go.
  - native/kernel_neon_arm64.s: the 4×4 (sixteen-accumulator) panel shape,
    following aikit's measurement that at least ten independent FMA chains
    are needed to reach FMA peak.
  - The CLS-only final layer, pooled forward scratch and head-parallel
    attention, after the corresponding aikit encoder techniques.

